Don't leave off-mesh links to a removed tile in tiles further away.

NS links off-mesh connections (phase gates) between any two tiles on the map
(dtNavMesh::GlobalOffMeshLinks), but removeTile() only unlinked the eight
neighbour tiles. When the tile cache rebuilt a tile, for example after a
structure was placed on it, the tile at the other end of a phase gate kept a
link to a poly of the old tile. findPath() follows links with
getTileAndPolyByRefUnsafe(), so it read a poly index past the new tile's
polys and crashed (seen on ns_45_beta3: commander move order -> findPath,
poly 4 of a 2-poly tile).

removeTile() now unlinks every tile, and the tile cache marks the off-mesh
connections that start or end in a rebuilt tile dirty, so update() links
them to the new tile again.

--- a/main/source/detour/DetourNavMesh.cpp
+++ b/main/source/detour/DetourNavMesh.cpp
@@ -1603,7 +1603,16 @@
 		for (int j = 0; j < nneis; ++j)
 			unconnectLinks(neis[j], tile);
 	}
-		
+
+	// Disconnect off-mesh links from tiles further away. Off-mesh connections
+	// (phase gates) are linked across the whole map by GlobalOffMeshLinks(),
+	// and a link left behind points at a poly of the old tile.
+	for (int i = 0; i < m_maxTiles; ++i)
+	{
+		if (&m_tiles[i] != tile && m_tiles[i].header)
+			unconnectLinks(&m_tiles[i], tile);
+	}
+
 	// Reset tile.
 	if (tile->flags & DT_TILE_FREE_DATA)
